From e96d22b0720b4009393728040753abd083ee8cae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:27:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(core-update): a paused turn continues in place once no
 successor backend is coming [daveey]

The in-place watcher waited LEAVE_GRACE_S (900 s) after the checkout moved for a
replacement backend that only comes once the skew watchdog proves the process idle.
A backend kept busy by other chats (or with no watchdog) never retires, so every
paused turn on it stalled 15-20 min (David-MBP 2026-10-28 07:03 -> 07:18).

Now the watcher hands off only while a replacement is coming (retirement fence
preparing/committed, or watchdog armed + idle proof true). No watchdog: continue
at once; blocked for NO_REPLACEMENT_S (60 s): continue here; backstop 300 s.
Settled turns (running/scheduled/marker gone) are 'done' before the skew check,
so a moved-on turn is never re-continued. The retirement fence keeps in-place and
successor continuation exclusive. (t_01a18300e42c3364)
